                            <comment id="16719482" author="githubbot" created="Wed, 12 Dec 2018 21:54:20 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;GitHub user aealeksandrov opened a pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/5658&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/5658&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-10657&quot; title=&quot;Thin clients (ODBC, JDBC, Java) should call ctx.security().onSessionExpired(subjid) on disconnect to avoid the possible leaking of the memory&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-10657&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-10657&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: ctx.security().onSessionExpired method is now called on&#8230;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &#8230; thin clients disconnect.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    At the moment all classes that implement ClientListenerAbstractConnectionContext don&apos;t call the ctx.security().onSessionExpired(subjid) on disconect.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    It provides the leaking of the memory related to resources that were generated during authentification.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can merge this pull request into a Git repository by running:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    $ git pull &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/gridgain/apache-ignite&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/gridgain/apache-ignite&lt;/a&gt; ignite-10657&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Alternatively you can review and apply these changes as the patch at:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/5658.patch&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/5658.patch&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To close this pull request, make a commit to your master/trunk branch&lt;br/&gt;
with (at least) the following in the commit message:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    This closes #5658&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;p&gt;commit a169c338b4fd8b183b1f9489d312bf7e07fefcfd&lt;br/&gt;
Author: Andrei Aleksandrov &amp;lt;aealexsandrov@...&amp;gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Date:   2018-12-12T19:38:06Z&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-10657&quot; title=&quot;Thin clients (ODBC, JDBC, Java) should call ctx.security().onSessionExpired(subjid) on disconnect to avoid the possible leaking of the memory&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-10657&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-10657&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: ctx.security().onSessionExpired method is now called on thin clients disconnects.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;hr /&gt;</comment>
